---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy | AI Career Guide" description="How AI Career Guide researches, reviews, updates, and corrects its content.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 prose max-w-none prose-headings:text-[var(--color-text-primary)] prose-p:text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] prose-li:text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] prose-a:text-[var(--color-accent)]">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider !text-[var(--color-accent)]">Editorial standards</p>
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p>AI Career Guide aims to publish practical, accurate, and useful material about AI, software engineering, projects, and technology careers.</p>
    <h2>Research and sources</h2>
    <p>Technical articles should use reliable primary documentation, standards, official project documentation, or other reputable sources when factual claims require verification. Source links are included on articles when available.</p>
    <h2>Updates and reviews</h2>
    <p><strong>Published</strong> means the article was first released. <strong>Updated</strong> is reserved for meaningful content changes. <strong>Reviewed</strong> indicates an editorial check of the existing material; it does not imply that every external fact remains current indefinitely.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>When a material error is identified, the content should be corrected and, where appropriate, the update date changed. Readers can use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> to report a specific issue with a source.</p>
    <h2>Affiliate and commercial content</h2>
    <p>Commercial relationships should never determine technical conclusions. Any affiliate or sponsored relationship will be disclosed where applicable.</p>
    <h2>AI-assisted writing</h2>
    <p>AI tools may assist with drafting, editing, research organization, or code examples, but published material is expected to be reviewed for accuracy and usefulness before release.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
